  "title": "Walter W FDE 4834 NDE 4834",
  "date": "'Dec. 30, 1958'",
  "content": "After spending Christmas with my folks in Ohio, I set out at 5:00 am in my car to return to my apartment in Massachusetts. The weather was poor most of the way. Four hours out of Ohio, at 9:15 am, I was driving in snow and sleet, and a little too fast for the road conditions, when the car went into a skid. I began swerving toward an approaching car in the left lane. Not thinking, I stepped on the brake, turned the wheels to the right, slid sideways out of control back into the right lane, shot over the right embankment between two telephone poles, bounced into a field and across it, and ended up on a side road facing the highway! (The only physical damage to my car was the right front grill and bumper, which were bent into the right tire, which fortunately served to slow the vehicle and bring it to a stop.) The above background is necessary in order to understand just how helpless I felt as I crossed the highway and went down the embankment. I really felt that I was going to die! During this brief interval, I experienced the panoramic life review phenomenon - a horizontal series of TV- or movie-like screens of what I believe were past events in my life. Though I couldn't remember the content of any of these scenes afterward, I recall that they were very detailed. The strip of pictures seemed to move past quite rapidly.",
